# GoBD and retention

- Preserve confirmed costs, booked payments, released vouchers and finalized
  snapshots. Keep content and original files immutable, including in migrations.
- Correct a booking by reversal or an existing version/supersession path; retain
  the original, its references, checksum and audit trail. Never delete it to fix it.
- Preserve database immutability guards and add negative tests for changed paths,
  following `docs/adr/0003-gobd-immutability-mechanism.md`.
- Respect `retention_until` and existing retention-binding checks. GDPR operations
  restrict retained data instead of erasing or rewriting originals; use
  `docs/adr/0012-gdpr-erasure-vs-gobd-retention.md` and
  `backend/app/services/dsgvo_service.py`. Do not invent new retention policy.
